      "side": 0,
      "message": "Q:Can you help me understand why this CL affects behavior? Is there a race condition somewhere?\nA:Ok, because set_state() function in usb_pd_prtocol.c check if port partner is pd capable or not via receiving SRC_Cap or GoodCRC, and then enable (not pd capable) or disable (pd capable) the SLEEP_MASK_USB_PD again. This means that it83xx_tcpm_set_rx_enable() setting SLEEP_MASK_USB_PD value will be overwritten. So I add another global variable for sleep mode via checking rx enable or not, if SLEEP_MASK_USB_PD and pd_need_awake both allow turning off pd module clock then we can go to sleep mode.  \n\n\nQ:Or is the only bug fix needed on line 576? I think that one line change fixes the problem and nothing else is needed.\nA:No, we need fix both enable/disable sleep mode and line 576.\nOnly fix line 576, the SLEEP_MASK_USB_PD will be overwritten by set_state(), then TCPC still miss messages from partner.",
